1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,640
Give every site of a three-dimensional
grid its own random energy.

2
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:06,910
Here we show one layer.

3
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:11,880
Now release a quantum wave.
When the disorder is strong,

4
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:13,930
the wave stays where it started.

5
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:18,100
But when the disorder is weak,
in three or more dimensions,

6
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:20,290
some waves should travel forever.

7
00:00:21,410 --> 00:00:25,640
Proving this has long resisted
mathematics. Here is a claimed proof,

8
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:27,930
and what a proof checker has verified.

9
00:00:30,333 --> 00:00:31,933
The setting is the Anderson model.

10
00:00:32,733 --> 00:00:34,733
The sites form the integer
lattice in d dimensions.

11
00:00:35,293 --> 00:00:37,153
A wave assigns a number to every site.

12
00:00:37,673 --> 00:00:41,133
The operator H acts on a wave u.
At each site n,

13
00:00:41,553 --> 00:00:43,993
it adds up the values of
u at the neighbours of n.

14
00:00:44,503 --> 00:00:49,643
Then it adds V of n, times u of n.
Here V of n is the energy of site n.

15
00:00:50,163 --> 00:00:53,833
The energies are independent random
numbers, uniform between a and b.

16
00:00:54,193 --> 00:00:58,703
The width, b minus a, measures the
disorder. We call half the width lambda.

17
00:00:59,183 --> 00:01:00,753
Every wave has a spectral measure.

18
00:01:01,473 --> 00:01:03,333
It spreads the wave's
weight over the energies.

19
00:01:03,863 --> 00:01:07,513
Point masses are eigenvalues;
their eigenvectors are bound states.

20
00:01:08,033 --> 00:01:10,913
The part with a density is the
absolutely continuous part.

21
00:01:11,473 --> 00:01:13,743
It is carried by states that
spread through the lattice.

22
00:01:14,273 --> 00:01:17,773
In the year two thousand,
Barry Simon listed this as Problem one.

23
00:01:18,313 --> 00:01:20,673
In three or more dimensions,
for suitable disorder,

24
00:01:21,193 --> 00:01:25,023
prove purely absolutely continuous
spectrum in some range of energies.

25
00:01:25,503 --> 00:01:29,453
Purely means no eigenvalues,
and no singular part, in that range.

26
00:01:30,073 --> 00:01:33,023
And the range must lie in the spectrum,
with nonzero weight.

27
00:01:35,433 --> 00:01:39,493
Every proved result about the kind of
spectrum on the lattice pointed the other

28
00:01:39,493 --> 00:01:43,893
way. In one dimension, all states
are localized. In any dimension,

29
00:01:44,273 --> 00:01:46,593
strong disorder gives localization too,

30
00:01:46,913 --> 00:01:49,383
and so do energies near
the edge of the spectrum.

31
00:01:49,763 --> 00:01:54,133
Extended states had been proved only
on trees, such as the Bethe lattice.

32
00:01:54,873 --> 00:01:57,843
That was the work of Abel Klein,
in the nineteen nineties.

33
00:01:58,263 --> 00:02:04,013
The main tool is the Green function,
G of z. It is the inverse of H minus z.

34
00:02:04,733 --> 00:02:08,293
Here z is an energy E,
plus a small imaginary part, eta.

35
00:02:09,533 --> 00:02:10,633
Eta acts as a damping.

36
00:02:11,583 --> 00:02:15,073
On a tree, removing one site splits
the graph into independent branches.

37
00:02:15,953 --> 00:02:18,993
So the Green function at that
site obeys an exact recursion,

38
00:02:19,313 --> 00:02:20,333
in terms of the branches.

39
00:02:21,223 --> 00:02:25,853
On the lattice, loops tie the neighbours
back together. No such equation closes.

40
00:02:27,023 --> 00:02:30,373
Perturbation theory follows the
wave for long, but finite, times,

41
00:02:30,373 --> 00:02:33,373
of order lambda to the
minus two minus kappa.

42
00:02:34,493 --> 00:02:38,633
Here kappa is a small positive number.
As the disorder goes to zero,

43
00:02:38,853 --> 00:02:43,353
after rescaling, the averaged density
of the wave spreads like heat over those

44
00:02:43,353 --> 00:02:47,003
times. That is the work of Erdős,
Salmhofer and Yau.

45
00:02:48,053 --> 00:02:51,613
Following a wave up to some time is
comparable to damping the Green function

46
00:02:51,613 --> 00:02:52,973
by one over that time.

47
00:02:53,673 --> 00:02:57,583
So these results correspond to a damping
of about lambda to the two plus kappa.

48
00:02:58,363 --> 00:03:02,793
But spectral type is a statement about
all times. The damping must go to zero,

49
00:03:02,793 --> 00:03:06,423
at fixed disorder.
That last limit is the obstacle.

50
00:03:08,833 --> 00:03:14,153
In September twenty twenty-six, OpenAI
posted a manuscript of ninety-three pages.

51
00:03:15,153 --> 00:03:19,273
It claims a proof for the uniform model,
in every dimension from three up.

52
00:03:19,973 --> 00:03:21,963
It has not been independently refereed.

53
00:03:22,823 --> 00:03:25,693
Its Theorem one point
one centres the energies,

54
00:03:26,173 --> 00:03:30,413
so they lie between minus lambda
and lambda. For small enough lambda,

55
00:03:30,953 --> 00:03:35,493
almost surely, a fixed interval just
above the bottom of the band lies in the

56
00:03:35,493 --> 00:03:39,313
spectrum. And there, the spectrum
is purely absolutely continuous.

57
00:03:39,833 --> 00:03:43,853
Here is the plan of the argument,
as a map. Each box is a stage,

58
00:03:44,233 --> 00:03:48,513
and we will visit them in order.
Everything aims at one finite certificate.

59
00:03:49,163 --> 00:03:51,593
The certificate lives
on a large periodic box.

60
00:03:52,373 --> 00:03:54,533
Add a tiny damping on at
least half of the sites.

61
00:03:55,393 --> 00:03:59,133
Then the Green function at those sites
keeps an imaginary part bounded below,

62
00:03:59,653 --> 00:04:03,293
however large the box.
And the damping shrinks as the box grows.

63
00:04:03,933 --> 00:04:07,873
A lower bound that survives as the
damping goes to zero is the signature of

64
00:04:07,873 --> 00:04:09,443
absolutely continuous spectrum.

65
00:04:10,133 --> 00:04:13,693
To build the certificate, the construction
starts with no disorder at all.

66
00:04:14,293 --> 00:04:17,573
Then it reveals each random
energy one binary digit at a time.

67
00:04:18,293 --> 00:04:19,513
Each digit is a fair coin,

68
00:04:19,513 --> 00:04:23,123
and moves the energy up or
down by half the previous step.

69
00:04:23,893 --> 00:04:26,233
The digits not yet revealed
are replaced by a damping,

70
00:04:26,333 --> 00:04:28,273
of the same size as their variance.

71
00:04:28,713 --> 00:04:31,433
It is a mean-field stand-in
for the hidden disorder.

72
00:04:31,433 --> 00:04:35,173
Each revealed digit trades
damping for true randomness.

73
00:04:35,758 --> 00:04:40,818
Three controls are carried through every
stage. First, at the end of each stage,

74
00:04:41,158 --> 00:04:44,258
the damping at each site must match
the Green function it produces.

75
00:04:45,018 --> 00:04:46,938
That self-consistent
equation can be restored,

76
00:04:46,938 --> 00:04:51,218
because its feedback stays below one
third, together with further bounds.

77
00:04:52,118 --> 00:04:55,758
Second, no row of the Green function
concentrates on a few sites.

78
00:04:56,258 --> 00:04:58,058
So no single update can move much.

79
00:04:58,578 --> 00:05:01,578
Third, an exact identity,
the Ward identity,

80
00:05:02,098 --> 00:05:04,218
turns the Green function
into a weighted graph.

81
00:05:04,578 --> 00:05:08,808
Its Laplacian adds up many small
local changes into one bound.

82
00:05:09,458 --> 00:05:13,418
Updates are tested on finite tiles.
A failed trial is rolled back.

83
00:05:13,998 --> 00:05:15,338
Its sites are marked pending.

84
00:05:15,848 --> 00:05:18,458
Later, small clusters of
pending sites are cleared.

85
00:05:19,158 --> 00:05:22,818
A scattering matrix identifies the
directions through which a cluster reaches

86
00:05:22,818 --> 00:05:23,938
the sites around it.

87
00:05:24,398 --> 00:05:28,298
When those directions carry only
weak weight at every remaining site,

88
00:05:28,878 --> 00:05:31,468
completing the cluster changes
the rest only a little.

89
00:05:31,978 --> 00:05:36,278
With high probability, nothing is pending
at the end. The last digits go in,

90
00:05:36,598 --> 00:05:37,818
and the certificate holds.

91
00:05:38,338 --> 00:05:40,658
A final spectral argument
reads the certificate.

92
00:05:41,218 --> 00:05:45,198
It gives absolutely continuous spectrum
on the interval, almost surely,

93
00:05:45,718 --> 00:05:50,349
with no eigenvalues and no singular part.
That is Theorem one point one.

94
00:05:52,867 --> 00:05:55,567
So what is established?
Here is the ledger.

95
00:05:56,077 --> 00:06:00,417
Proved, and peer reviewed: localization,
in one dimension and at strong disorder.

96
00:06:01,677 --> 00:06:06,477
Extended states on trees. And diffusion up
to long, finite times, in a scaling limit.

97
00:06:07,337 --> 00:06:11,297
Claimed: the manuscript itself.
Its text has not been refereed.

98
00:06:12,157 --> 00:06:14,757
Checked by the Lean proof assistant:
the whole argument,

99
00:06:14,757 --> 00:06:19,977
formalized from start to finish. It
proves Theorem one point one, and from it,

100
00:06:20,297 --> 00:06:22,207
a precise statement of Simon's problem.

101
00:06:22,977 --> 00:06:24,857
And the pictures in this
film are explanations,

102
00:06:25,757 --> 00:06:28,807
including the mean-field reading
of the damping. They prove nothing.

103
00:06:29,597 --> 00:06:32,997
In short: Simon's Problem one,
as formalized in Lean,

104
00:06:33,377 --> 00:06:37,957
has a complete machine-checked proof. The
manuscript behind it is still unrefereed.

105
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:44,520
Here is the plan again.
Every box is formalized in Lean,

106
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:49,720
and every step is proved.
A blue seal marks a proved box.

107
00:06:50,510 --> 00:06:53,160
Two boxes follow Theorem one point one.

108
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:56,360
The first restates it
in Simon's conventions.

109
00:06:57,160 --> 00:07:00,900
The second is Simon's problem,
stated with Mathlib alone,

110
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:03,730
the standard library
of formal mathematics.

111
00:07:04,550 --> 00:07:07,520
In all, the proof has eight
hundred and fifty-three files,

112
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:09,350
with no unfinished steps.

113
00:07:10,645 --> 00:07:15,725
Now the final statement, clause by clause.
In every dimension d of at least three,

114
00:07:16,245 --> 00:07:17,875
there is a width bound, delta.

115
00:07:18,555 --> 00:07:21,425
For every interval from a
to b narrower than delta,

116
00:07:22,025 --> 00:07:25,202
there is an open energy interval,
from E one to E two.

117
00:07:26,442 --> 00:07:31,865
Take any independent family of energies,
uniform on a to b. Then, almost surely,

118
00:07:32,265 --> 00:07:33,605
the operator exists,

119
00:07:33,925 --> 00:07:35,845
the energy interval lies in its spectrum,

120
00:07:36,465 --> 00:07:39,185
every spectral measure is
absolutely continuous there,

121
00:07:39,245 --> 00:07:41,915
and some wave has nonzero weight there.

122
00:07:42,835 --> 00:07:46,565
The final theorem uses only
Lean's three standard axioms.

123
00:07:47,905 --> 00:07:52,445
Lean's replay tool checked every
step again, from scratch. And nanoda,

124
00:07:52,705 --> 00:07:54,265
an independently written checker,

125
00:07:54,885 --> 00:07:57,625
confirmed that the proved statement
matches an independent copy.

126
00:07:58,525 --> 00:08:00,785
In a control, two replaces three.

127
00:08:01,325 --> 00:08:03,585
Then the statement no longer
matches the one proved.

128
00:08:04,565 --> 00:08:06,505
The proof covers three dimensions and up.

129
00:08:07,375 --> 00:08:10,945
Formalizing every step found one
literal omission in the manuscript.

130
00:08:10,945 --> 00:08:15,445
Its Lemma six point two needs the
damping scale to be at most one.

131
00:08:16,525 --> 00:08:18,315
That holds wherever the lemma is used.

132
00:08:19,195 --> 00:08:22,865
What does the check not certify?
That these definitions say what we claim;

133
00:08:23,485 --> 00:08:24,985
you can judge that by reading them.

134
00:08:25,585 --> 00:08:27,485
The correctness of the
library's own definitions.

135
00:08:28,325 --> 00:08:29,905
And every sentence of the manuscript.

136
00:08:30,845 --> 00:08:35,405
One more caution. The exported statement
lets the energy interval depend on the

137
00:08:35,405 --> 00:08:39,365
width, b minus a.
Theorem one point one fixes the interval,

138
00:08:39,905 --> 00:08:43,645
just above the bottom of the band.
That fixed form is proved too,

139
00:08:44,085 --> 00:08:48,075
but it is stated in the terms of
OpenAI's Lean library, not Mathlib alone.

140
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:55,190
Even granting the theorem,
much remains open. The full mobility edge.

141
00:08:55,910 --> 00:09:00,910
Quantum diffusion. Two dimensions.
Other random laws. And explicit constants.

